WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:03.944
Roxy watched as Cozlin and Sapphire fought two aliens.

2
00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:05.939
One alien had bat wings.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.867
The other one looked like a cloud.

4
00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:12.017
The cloud swirled around Cozlin.

5
00:00:12.018 --> 00:00:17.787
"Ugh!" Cozlin cried. "I'm getting dizzy!"

6
00:00:17.788 --> 00:00:22.311
She moved fast, darting across the stadium while the cloud still swirled.

7
00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:25.784
Sapphire swooped down, blasting the cloud with flames.

8
00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:29.236
When the smoke cleared, the cloud was gone.

9
00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:33.127
The bat gulped. "I surrender!"

10
00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:38.768
"The winners are Kid Comet and the dragon!" the Battle Master said.

11
00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:44.247
The crowd cheered.

12
00:00:44.248 --> 00:00:48.873
*** A chipmunk sniffed the bronze door in the

13
00:00:48.874 --> 00:00:51.764
mountains. Suddenly light sparkled, and a portal

14
00:00:51.765 --> 00:00:53.802
opened. The chipmunk hurried

15
00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:59.778
away. Terrell, Bajie, and the bird stepped out of the

16
00:00:59.779 --> 00:01:01.108
portal. Bippo followed

17
00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:06.219
them. "Here's the door." Terrell pushed, but it didn't

18
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:11.025
open. "Stand back, Terrell!" Bajie swung his rake.

19
00:01:11.026 --> 00:01:13.904
Clang! The rake rattled, shaking Bajie until he dropped it.

20
00:01:13.905 --> 00:01:16.185
The door was still closed.

21
00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:21.653
"Bippo," Terrell said. "Can you open a portal to get us inside?"

22
00:01:21.654 --> 00:01:28.774
"There's no need." The bird muttered a spell, and the door swung open.

23
00:01:28.775 --> 00:01:32.341
Bajie grabbed his rake, and everyone went inside.

24
00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:38.194
A long corridor led them to a large, empty chamber.

25
00:01:38.195 --> 00:01:40.619
Terrell looked at the old vase.

26
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.799
"I don't understand. I thought Guanyin was going to help—"

27
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:50.426
Rumble! Rumble! The chamber shook, sending pieces of rock crashing down.

28
00:01:50.427 --> 00:01:52.851
Bajie fell over. "Oof!"

29
00:01:52.852 --> 00:01:56.576
Terrell gulped. "It's another earthquake!"

30
00:01:56.577 --> 00:02:00.449
The bird tipped the vase, and gold coins poured out.

31
00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.728
Right away the earthquake grew weaker.

32
00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:05.124
The bird flew around, pouring coins.

33
00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:08.065
They formed large piles all over the chamber.

34
00:02:08.066 --> 00:02:11.792
As the last coin rolled out, the shaking stopped completely.

35
00:02:11.793 --> 00:02:16.545
"Whoa!" Terrell stared at the vase. "I can't believe . . ."

36
00:02:16.546 --> 00:02:21.346
Light sparkled, and the bird disappeared. A woman stood in its place.

37
00:02:21.347 --> 00:02:27.606
Bajie bowed and chuckled. "I knew that was you, Bodhisattva!"

38
00:02:27.607 --> 00:02:32.235
Terrell gasped. "You're the bodhisattva Guanyin!"

39
00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:36.940
Guanyin smiled. "Yes, and this is the gold that was stolen.

40
00:02:36.941 --> 00:02:42.854
Balance has been restored, and there will be no more earthquakes."

41
00:02:42.855 --> 00:02:47.568
The group went back outside, and the massive door closed gently behind them.

42
00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:49.715
"Thank you," Terrell said.

43
00:02:49.716 --> 00:02:52.452
"You're welcome," Guanyin said.

44
00:02:52.453 --> 00:02:56.376
"Yeah, no problem at all!" Bajie grinned.

45
00:02:56.377 --> 00:02:59.109
Then he and the bodhisattva vanished.

46
00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.127
Terrell was about to call Dr. Odd when he heard heavy footsteps approaching.

47
00:03:03.128 --> 00:03:06.827
He spun around and saw Dr. Odd's robot running toward him.

48
00:03:06.828 --> 00:03:09.557
"I was just about to call you," Terrell said.

49
00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:11.685
"We stopped the earthquakes!"

50
00:03:11.686 --> 00:03:14.698
"Excellent work, Terrell," Dr. Odd said. "Now

51
00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:19.818
come with me. It's time to save our friends!" ***

52
00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:22.973
"Where are we going?" Terrell asked.

53
00:03:22.974 --> 00:03:26.137
They were in a small spaceship, orbiting Earth.

54
00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:31.428
Dr. Odd smiled. "Far away. We'll need my moon."

55
00:03:31.429 --> 00:03:35.398
Soon the spaceship was docked in one of the moon's hangars.

56
00:03:35.399 --> 00:03:42.745
They went to the control room, where Dr. Odd pressed some buttons.

57
00:03:42.746 --> 00:03:45.359
The moon shook for a moment.

58
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.759
"What just happened?" Terrell asked.

59
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.679
"We went through a portal." Dr. Odd pressed some more buttons.

60
00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.981
"We are now millions of light-years from Earth."

61
00:03:59.982 --> 00:04:04.145
The moon rotated, and Terrell saw a strange space station.

62
00:04:04.146 --> 00:04:08.226
Platforms surrounded it. They were filled with spaceships.

63
00:04:08.227 --> 00:04:13.704
Terrell scratched his head. "That looks like a . . . stadium."

64
00:04:13.705 --> 00:04:16.278
Dr. Odd nodded, looking grim.

65
00:04:16.279 --> 00:04:23.938
"That's where our friends are. It's called the Stadium of the Stars."

